  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mi>III</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mi>IV</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mi>II</mi></mfenced></math><p>Caesium is used in devising photoelectric cells. Boron fibres are used in making bullet-proof vest. Silicones being surrounded by non-polar alkyl groups are water repelling in nature. Gallium is less toxic and has a very high boiling point, so it is used in high temperature thermometers.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Column I<br />\t\t\t(Element)</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Column II<br />\t\t\t(Uses)</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>i</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cs</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>c</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;Photoelectric cell</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>ii</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ga</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>a</td>\t\t\t<td>High temperature thermometer</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>iii</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>d</td>\t\t\t<td>Bullet-proof vest</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>iv</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Si</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>b</td>\t\t\t<td>Water repellent sprays</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>"
